# Cursor Editor — Tab Autocompletions

## Overview

Cursor's Tab autocompletion feature provides AI-powered inline code suggestions as you type. Unlike traditional completion engines (such as GitHub Copilot), Cursor's Tab understands your **full project context** — not just the current file, but all open files, recently edited files, and the broader project structure.

Tab completions are generated by the Cursor model (configurable per provider) and appear as gray ghost text in the editor that can be accepted with a single keypress.

### Tab vs Cursor Composer

| Aspect | Tab Autocompletion | Composer (Cmd+K/L) |
|--------|-------------------|-------------------|
| **Trigger** | Automatic (as you type) | Manual (Cmd+K or Cmd+L) |
| **Scope** | Single line or word completion | Multi-line edits, full code blocks |
| **Interaction** | Press Tab to accept, right-arrow for next word | Submit prompt, review diff, accept/reject |
| **Model usage** | Lighter model (Haiku, GPT-3.5, local) | Full agent model (Sonnet, GPT-4, Opus) |
| **Context window** | Smaller, focused on current file | Larger, includes full project context |

