## Acceptance Behavior

### Key Controls

| Key | Action | Description |
|-----|--------|-------------|
| `Tab` | Accept full completion | Inserts the entire suggested text |
| `Ctrl+Right` (Mac: `Cmd+Right`) | Accept next word | Inserts only the next word of the suggestion |
| `Escape` | Dismiss | Hides the current suggestion |
| `Down Arrow` | Next suggestion | Cycles through alternative completions |
| `Up Arrow` | Previous suggestion | Cycles through alternatives in reverse |
| `Ctrl+Enter` (Mac: `Cmd+Enter`) | Trigger new completion | Forces a fresh completion regardless of ghost text |
| `Ctrl+.` (Mac: `Cmd+.`) | Completion menu | Shows all available completions |

### Acceptance Visual Feedback

- **Ghost text**: Appears in gray in the editor, indicating it is suggested, not committed
- **Completion cursor**: When the first word is accepted, the completion cursor moves forward
- **Full acceptance**: When Tab is pressed, ghost text turns to normal text (black)

### Smart Acceptance

Cursor's Tab completions support smart partial acceptance:

```typescript
// User has typed this:
function calculateTotal(items: Item[]) {

// Tab completion suggests:
//   return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price * item.quantity, 0);

// User presses Tab:
// Full completion is inserted
```

