## Tab vs Traditional Completions

### Differences from GitHub Copilot

| Aspect | Cursor Tab | GitHub Copilot |
|--------|-----------|---------------|
| **Context** | Full project awareness | File-level + some workspace |
| **Model** | Configurable per user | Cursor's default |
| **Speed** | Optimized for low latency | Variable |
| **Integration** | Deep Cursor editor integration | VS Code extension |
| **Customization** | User-configurable models, endpoints | Fixed model selection |

### Differences from Traditional IDE Autocomplete

| Aspect | Cursor Tab | Traditional Autocomplete |
|--------|-----------|-------------------------|
| **Generation** | AI-generated from language model | Keyword/AST-based matching |
| **Context scope** | Semantic understanding of code | Syntactic matching |
| **Multi-line** | Can suggest multiple lines | Usually single line |
| **Adaptation** | Learns from project patterns | Static, no learning |
| **Language support** | Any language the model understands | Language-specific engines |

