## Troubleshooting

### Completions Not Appearing

| Cause | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| `editor.tabAutocompletion` is `false` | Set to `true` in settings |
| No API key configured | Set API key in Cursor Settings > Model Provider |
| Model not available | Check provider is reachable; verify model ID |
| Too many open files | Close unnecessary tabs to free context |
| File type excluded | Check `excludeFileTypes` setting |
| Min input length too high | Reduce `minInputLength` to 1 or 2 |

### Slow Completions

| Cause | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| Large model selected for Tab | Switch to Haiku or GPT-3.5 |
| Network latency to API | Use local model (Ollama) or closer endpoint |
| Too much context | Close open files, reduce `minInputLength` |
| Debounce too low | Increase `debounce` to 200-300ms |

### Wrong Context in Completions

| Cause | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| Outdated open tabs | Reopen files after changes |
| Stale cache | Dismiss and re-trigger with `Cmd+Enter` |
| Wrong file context | Close irrelevant files; keep only related tabs open |
| Model hallucination | Accept partial and correct; the model improves over time |

### Ghost Text Not Dismissed

| Cause | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| Cursor lost focus | Press `Escape` or continue typing |
| Network timeout | Re-trigger with `Cmd+Enter` |
| Model error | Check API key and provider status |

